{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfSQRPnmJsE5A88dn8kYt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 08 is complete: code, tests, report section, tables, PROGRESS.md and iterations.md are all written, and nothing was committed or written to `solutions/`.\n\n**What was built**\n- `learning/treewidth.c` and `learning/treewidth.py`: exact treewidth by the subset DP to 26 vertices and by a decision search with simplicial reductions to 64, each answer carrying a re-checkable elimination ordering.\n- `learning/extremal.py`: the bit-flip local search with the exact solver as oracle, nauty deduplication, five objectives, three seed families, the corpus treewidth pass, and re-certification of every draw by solver, both refutation configurations, lattice oracle and pathwidth DP.\n- `tests/test_extremal.py`: 22 tests. Full suite passes with 968 tests in 82 s.\n\n**What was found** (`reports/ml_nature.md` §21, `reports/extremal_tables.md`)\n- **Kill not met** on four of five objectives. The search beats the corpus's worst instance at the same size on gap, on pathwidth minus treewidth, on refutation nodes (3 to 12 times), and on `cs-dfs` overshoot. It is met for the soundness objective: zero wrong answers in 727,816 evaluations.\n- **The smallest known instance with `pw − tw ≥ 2` has 10 vertices**: three K4s glued pairwise at three hub vertices plus one vertex tied to each. Treewidth 3, pathwidth 5, vertex-minimal and edge-minimal, proved by a K4, an elimination ordering, two refutations, the pathwidth DP and the lattice oracle. The corpus's smallest has 19 vertices and the smallest tree needs 22.\n- **§6's floor is now an interval.** Of the 338 gap ≥ 2 corpus instances, pathwidth exceeds treewidth on 164, equals it on 80, and 94 are open, mostly above 64 customers where the decision search does not reach.\n- `pw − tw` grows with n but slowly: 1 at 7 vertices, 2 at 10, and 3 not below 50 customers on any record.